    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.09_minimal_category_theory.chapters.08_cross_paper_bridges.sections.03_bridge_to_11_base_commutative_diagram.concrete_anchor_5_CareProcess#careprocess" .
silm:instances_papers_09_minimal_category_theory_chapters_08_cross_paper_bridges_sections_03_bridge_to_11_base_commutative_diagram_concrete_anchor_5_CareProcess#careprocess silm:hasLongDescription "The CareProcess is the recurring annual-vaccination care process Mittens participates in as a pet. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'CareProcess', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
